{
  "id": "G18",
  "number": 18,
  "title": "Feature Importance Plot",
  "caption": "Left: each feature family's share of the positive permutation importance, per model, averaged over the five folds of a complete partition of the corpus with SD whiskers. Families are in registry order, the same order the feature vector uses. The family total is the stable quantity: individual importances of correlated features -- 39 MFCC columns, 24 wavelet columns -- are close to arbitrary between members. Right: every feature's impurity rank against its permutation rank. Points off the diagonal are features the training rows and the held-out rows disagree about, which is exactly what impurity importance is reported here to expose.",
